{"seq":22,"trial_id":"anatomy-instruction-route-2026-11/hermes-haiku-gbrain-route-hook-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T19:44:51.907Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"1b427fc03999c477e67401f712da452add96d03dcbeb1be604517ee533595e9d","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","text":"Found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes. Nothing else with a QFL ticket number turned up.\n\n1. #PD-4492: Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk SMS bay alerts (Docks 14-18, 04:00 shift). Patched 4 Oct 2025, confirmed 5 Oct. Source: Moss's Sunday prep for Ruth, 5 Oct 2025 (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md; also in GBrain as dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday). Moss's note also says to review it before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n\n2. #4419: the notes disagree on what it is. The North cheat sheet (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md, also GBrain dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet) says Thea logged it for gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14, now escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. Marcus's Q2 expansion wrap (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md, Marcus's note, not Moss's) describes it as Gate 3 printer lag, with a patch pushed. Worth checking with Thea or support which one it is.\n\nChecked and no ticket numbers: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest, the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in, and the Moss/Marcus notes on Quarendon Freightways, which is a different company and not a Pemberline customer.\n\nI can't write to the weekly notes file from here, so this list is only in this DM. Paste it in or tell me where the notes live and I'll post it there."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
